module bindings.rust.unapproved_login_artifact_authentication;

// A passwordless login artifact is created at the requester's initiative:
// the requester names the account and holds the access code that identifies
// the request, so the artifact's shared secret alone authenticates the
// requester to the artifact, never the account holder to the server. The
// account holder's recorded approval -- and the account the artifact
// belongs to -- is what turns it into a credential, which is why the
// approval endpoint writes approved and user_uuid and the login path must
// read them.
//
// The AuthRequest model publishes every atom of the flow this recognises:
// AuthRequest::find_by_uuid resolves the stored request from a
// request-supplied identifier, check_access_code verifies the shared code,
// and check_valid_password is the primary credential check the artifact
// branch replaces. What is matched here is the login function -- the one
// that carries the primary credential check -- resolving the artifact and
// verifying its code while never reading the artifact's approval or owner
// fields. The atoms are the model's own names, answerable to the flow's
// documentation rather than to any one revision, and two non-login
// consumers stay unreported: the polling endpoint that answers the
// requesting device with the artifact's own state carries no primary
// credential check, and the approval endpoint writes the state the login
// must read.
//
// The judgement lives in the pack rule; this binding only recognises the
// atoms. Every clause is an exact call token or a selector match over the
// consuming function's own context, so prose in a comment satisfies neither
// side and a sibling function's approval read does not clear the login.

binding unapprovedLoginArtifactAuthentication {
  query pattern presenceNode where node.scope == "function" and node.context.language == "rust" and node.context.call in ["find_by_uuid"] and node.context.call in ["check_access_code"] and node.context.call in ["check_valid_password"] and not (containsAny(node.context.selector, ["approved", "user_uuid"]))
  emit issue code.UnapprovedLoginArtifactAuthentication at node
}
